Sorry, Rock. I didn't mean to toss you.

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:55.000
I'm Hal, by the way. Nice to meet you.

00:18:02.380 --> 00:18:04.360
Easy, my friend. Don't be in such a hurry.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:05.780
You'll forget where you already looked.

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:07.600
You don't want to go over the same area twice.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:09.080
Weeks.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.860
Oh, careful. You gotta gently pry off the top layer.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.160
You don't want to damage a fossil.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:44.340
Come on, is it a fossil?

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:47.350
No, it's not a fossil.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.610
It's just a different kind of rock inside the rock.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:51.940
Squeaks, my sweet little mouse.

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.200
The sun is still shining

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:54.900
and it's not time for your meeting yet.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:56.240
We can keep looking.

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.280
We can!

00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:59.680
A Mousy Scout never gives up!

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:09.800
Let's dig this fossil finding montage could sure use some music you track 17, please start 34 seconds in if you can

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:35.030
Mwah, mwah, mwah.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:13.720
No. Ow. No.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:18.170
Hey, Squeaks. I think we've got to call it a day.

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:19.570
It's getting dark.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:20.670
Oh, man.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.640
I guess I won't get my fossil badge after all tonight.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.840
Oh, we tried, Squeaks.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.760
We looked really, really, really hard to find a fossil.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:29.980
And I learned...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.120
how to stack rocks.

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:32.280
Ta-dee!

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:35.060
Really nice work, Hal!

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:38.010
Yeah, but you should probably put those rocks back

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:39.570
the way they were when you found them.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:42.100
Remember, leave nothing, take nothing.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:42.980
Ba-bam!

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.190
Thank you so much for helping, you guys.

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:50.110
Okay, so I didn't get a fossil badge.

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:52.860
Now, Biggie, I could go for a different badge.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:55.540
I could go for a cheese-eating badge.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:56.940
I'm good at eating cheese.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.510
I could do that, but...

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.510
It's not the same here.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:05.410
I wish we could have found a fossil for Squeaks.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:07.810
Well, maybe we can come back tomorrow.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.650
Yeah, I mean, there's a lot more rocks to stack.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.810
Like this one.

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:13.010
I must have missed it.

00:21:13.090 --> 00:21:14.150
I didn't even see that one.

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:15.980
Oh, let me see that.

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:18.040
Could it be?

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:19.240
Could it...

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:21.140
What is it?

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:33.980
You rang?

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:35.120
Uh...

00:21:35.430 --> 00:21:36.290
Uh...

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:38.050
Is this a fossil?

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:45.280
It's a fossil!

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:51.170
Fossil is called a trilobite!

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:52.840
A trilobite?

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:55.070
Oh, a real trilobite!

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:56.790
I can't believe we found a trilobite!

00:21:57.630 --> 00:21:59.950
What is a trilobite?

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.740
Trilobites lived in the ocean more than 300 million years ago!

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:07.240
Whoa-ho-ho-ho! That's so long a time ago!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:11.950
So, instead of a lake, there was an ancient ocean here!

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:14.070
Gimme some whaaaaaat!

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:16.850
This is like totally blood on the line, huh?

00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:18.910
Totally what she said, man!

00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:22.330
Now, mind of this!

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:25.100
Trilobites like to eat smaller plants and animals

00:22:25.100 --> 00:22:26.660
that lived in the ocean back then!

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:29.500
And there are none alive now!

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.330
Well, Squeaks, it looks like you're going to get your fossil badge after all!

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:36.150
Low vibe.

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:43.540
For the record, this bone is for next Friday.

00:22:44.020 --> 00:22:45.220
No, wait, next Thursday.

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:46.100
Okay, wait, no.

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:46.560
You know what?

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:47.240
Next Tuesday.

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:48.440
Do I hear Monday?

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:49.760
Next Monday, maybe?

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:51.120
Understood, Hal.

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:52.260
We've got your back!

00:22:52.420 --> 00:22:53.220
And your bone!

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:21.000
Nature Cat, Squeaks, Daisy, and Hal are cartoon characters

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.440
and not real animals.

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:24.940
To keep all of our animal friends safe,

00:23:25.240 --> 00:23:27.180
check with a grown up before you bring a pet

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:28.860
on your next nature adventure.

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:30.910
HAHA!
